WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.132
Flipping your class?

2
00:00:02.182 --> 00:00:03.873
You don't need a studio.

3
00:00:03.923 --> 00:00:09.436
The lecture slides you already have can become short pre-class videos your students will actually watch.

4
00:00:09.950 --> 00:00:13.708
Your slides are already sequenced and matched to your learning outcomes.

5
00:00:13.758 --> 00:00:20.385
As videos, students can pause and rewatch, read captions, and hear the same explanation every time.

6
00:00:20.885 --> 00:00:24.167
Plan short videos, not recorded lectures.

7
00:00:24.217 --> 00:00:32.319
A week on supply and demand becomes four short videos, one concept each, and each one names what students will do in class.

8
00:00:32.819 --> 00:00:37.390
Trim each slide to the key idea and move explanations into your notes.

9
00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:42.721
Those notes become the narration, so write them for the ear, and end with a link to class.

10
00:00:43.221 --> 00:00:49.173
Put each video in Moodle, Canvas or Blackboard, right beside the activity that depends on it.

11
00:00:49.223 --> 00:00:54.016
And tell students the viewing time up front: twelve minutes of video before Tuesday.

12
00:00:54.516 --> 00:00:57.752
Start with one week and make two or three short videos.

13
00:00:57.802 --> 00:01:03.173
Try Basic first, or let Pro's a.i. direct your deck into a produced explainer.

14
00:01:03.223 --> 00:01:08.109
Ordinary slides in, extraordinary video out at powerpoint2vid.com.

